      "title": "ndarray, dtypes and shape: the mental model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ndarray, dtypes and shape: the mental model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What an ndarray is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==ndarray== = one contiguous memory block plus metadata",
                "Metadata: `dtype`, `shape`, `strides`",
                "Every element has the **same type**; a list can mix",
                "Fixed size: resizing makes a new array"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Shape and dtype",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`shape` is a tuple: `np.zeros((2,3)).shape == (2,3)`",
                "`ndim` = `len(shape)`; `size` = product of shape",
                "`dtype` sets bytes per element: `int64`, `float64`, `bool`",
                "`astype` returns a **new** array; `reshape` keeps the size, `-1` infers one dimension"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "a = np.zeros((2, 3))",
                "a.dtype                  # float64",
                "b = a.astype('float32')  # new array",
                "a.reshape(3, -1)         # shape (3, 2)",
                "a.reshape(4, -1)         # ValueError: size 6"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Upcasting and overflow",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Mixed inputs get one dtype: the widest wins",
                "Order: ==bool < int < float < string=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Input",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`[1, 2, 3]`",
                  "`int64`"
                ],
                [
                  "`[1, 2.5]`",
                  "`float64`"
                ],
                [
                  "`[1, 2.5, 'a']`",
                  "string array"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Silent overflow",
              "text": "`np.array([255], dtype=np.uint8) + 1` gives ==[0]== silently. A scalar overflow warns instead, and in NumPy 1.x `np.uint8(255)+1` is 256."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Vectorised operations and broadcasting rules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Vectorised operations and broadcasting rules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Vectorised and ufuncs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Vectorised== = whole-array ops in compiled **C loops**",
                "`a * 2 + b` replaces a Python for-loop, ==10-100x== faster",
                "==Ufuncs== (`np.add`, `np.sqrt`, `np.exp`) apply elementwise",
                "`+`, `*`, `**` map to ufuncs; `*` is {red:elementwise}",
                "Matrix multiply: `a @ b` or `np.dot(a, b)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Broadcasting rule",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Align shapes",
                    "sub": "trailing dim first",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Missing dim",
                    "sub": "counts as 1",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Each pair",
                    "sub": "equal or one is 1",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "Else error",
                    "sub": "ValueError",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Shapes",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "(3,1) + (1,4)",
                  "{green:(3,4)}"
                ],
                [
                  "(5,3) + (3,)",
                  "{green:(5,3)}"
                ],
                [
                  "(3,) + (4,)",
                  "{red:ValueError}: operands could not be broadcast together"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotcha: (n,) vs (n,1)",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A (n,) vector with an (n,1) column silently gives ==(n,n)==",
                "Fix the shape: `a[:, None]` or `a.reshape(-1, 1)`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Check shapes first",
              "text": "No error does not mean the right answer: print `.shape` of both operands before adding."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Boolean masks and the axis argument",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Boolean masks and the axis argument",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Boolean masks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`mask = a > 5` gives a ==bool array== of the same shape",
                "`a[mask]` returns a **1-D** array of the True elements",
                "Combine with `&` `|` `~`, ==parentheses== round each test",
                "`and` / `or` on arrays raise {red:ValueError}",
                "`np.where(c, x, y)` picks x or y elementwise",
                "`np.where(c)` alone returns indices of True",
                "`mask.sum()` counts; `any()` / `all()` test"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import numpy as np",
                "a = np.array([1, 4, 7, 9, 2])",
                "print(a[(a > 2) & (a < 8)])",
                "print(np.where(a > 5)[0])",
                "print((a > 5).sum())"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[4 7]",
                "[2 3]",
                "2"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The axis argument",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call on (rows, cols)",
                "Collapses",
                "Gives"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`sum(axis=0)`",
                  "rows",
                  "one per ==column=="
                ],
                [
                  "`sum(axis=1)`",
                  "columns",
                  "one per ==row=="
                ],
                [
                  "`sum()` / `axis=None`",
                  "everything",
                  "one scalar"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`keepdims=True` keeps the reduced axis as size 1",
                "The result then ==broadcasts straight back=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "a = np.arange(6).reshape(2, 3)",
                "print(a.sum(axis=0))",
                "print(a.sum(axis=1))",
                "print(a - a.mean(axis=1, keepdims=True))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[3 5 7]",
                "[ 3 12]",
                "[[-1.  0.  1.]",
                " [-1.  0.  1.]]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`axis` names the dimension that **disappears**, not the one you keep."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Views vs copies and why pandas builds on NumPy",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Views vs copies and why pandas builds on NumPy",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Slices are views",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Basic slicing gives a ==view==: `a[1:4]`, `a[:, 0]`, `a.T`, `a.reshape(...)`",
                "Writing to a view ==changes the original=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import numpy as np",
                "a = np.arange(6)",
                "v = a[1:4]",
                "v[0] = 99",
                "print(a)",
                "print(np.shares_memory(a, v))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[ 0 99  2  3  4  5]",
                "True"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Copies and checks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Index",
                "Gives",
                "Writes a?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`a[1:4]`",
                  "view",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "`a[a > 5]`",
                  "copy",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`a[[0, 2]]`",
                  "copy",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`a[a > 5] = 0`",
                  "assignment",
                  "yes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Check: `np.shares_memory(a, b)` or `b.base is a`",
                "Fix: `b = a[1:4].copy()` stops accidental mutation"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. pandas builds on NumPy",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Columns are backed by ==NumPy arrays== with a dtype",
                "Inherit vector ops, masks `df[df.x > 5]`, `df.sum(axis=1)`; adds alignment",
                "Adds ==labelled index and columns==, per-column dtypes, NaN-aware missing data"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "to_numpy()",
              "text": "`.to_numpy()` may or may not be a view: ==copy before mutating=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "NumPy Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "NumPy Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Create and Reshape",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Do",
                "Call"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Create",
                  "`np.array(list)`, `np.zeros(shape)`, `np.ones(shape)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Ranges",
                  "`np.arange(0,10,2)`, `np.linspace(0,1,5)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Inspect",
                  "`a.shape` `a.dtype` `a.ndim` `a.size`"
                ],
                [
                  "Reshape",
                  "`a.reshape(r,-1)`, `a.T`, `a.ravel()`"
                ],
                [
                  "Convert",
                  "`a.astype(float)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Add axis",
                  "`np.newaxis` or `a[:, None]`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Broadcast, Mask, Axis",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Align shapes on the ==right==; each pair must be equal or 1",
                "`keepdims=True` on a reduction keeps shapes compatible"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "a - a.mean(axis=1, keepdims=True)"
              ],
              "note": "row means broadcast straight back"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Gives"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`a[(a>2)&(a<8)]`",
                  "True elements, 1-D"
                ],
                [
                  "`np.where(c,x,y)`",
                  "x or y per element"
                ],
                [
                  "`a.sum(axis=0)`",
                  "{green:per column}"
                ],
                [
                  "`a.sum(axis=1)`",
                  "{blue:per row}"
                ],
                [
                  "`a.mean()` `a.max()` `a.argmax()`",
                  "scalar, scalar, index"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Views vs Copies",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Slices are ==views==: writes change the original",
                "Masks and fancy indexing are **copies**",
                "`.copy()` makes a safe duplicate",
                "pandas wraps NumPy: `df.to_numpy()`, `df.values`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Axis is the dimension that gets ==collapsed==. Copy before you mutate."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
